    "title": "Tennis Season Kicks Off in Australia and New Zealand",
    "text": "•\tThe ATP and WTA tours are starting their 2026 season in Australia and New Zealand.\n•\tThe Australian Open begins January 18 in Melbourne.\n•\tThe United Cup, a mixed teams event, starts in Perth and Sydney on Friday and concludes January 11.\n•\tThe United Cup will feature top 10 players including Coco Gauff, Taylor Fritz, Alex de Minaur, Iga Swiątek, Alexander Zverev, Jasmine Paolini, and Felix Auger-Aliassime.\n•\tThe Brisbane International will feature defending champion Aryna Sabalenka.\n•\tCarlos Alcaraz and Jannik Sinner will participate in an exhibition in Incheon, South Korea, on January 10 and then travel to Australia.\n•\tAlcaraz will compete in his first major without coach Juan Carlos Ferrero.\n•\tOther players at the United Cup include Emma Raducanu, Naomi Osaka, Stefanos Tsitsipas, and Stan Wawrinka.\n•\tStan Wawrinka has announced that 2026 will be his final year on tour.\n•\tThe Brisbane International will also include Amanda Anisimova, Elena Rybakina, Madison Keys, Jessica Pegula, and Mirra Andreeva.\n•\tThe Adelaide International will feature Novak Djokovic from January 12-17.\n•\tThere will be a WTA 250 tournament in Hobart, Australia.\n•\tAuckland, New Zealand, will host a WTA tournament from January 5-11 and an ATP event from January 12-17.\n•\tKyrgios and Frances Tiafoe will play in an exhibition tournament at Kooyong in Melbourne.\n•\tHong Kong will host an ATP event from January 5-11.\n•\tATP events will implement a new rule for 10-minute breaks during extreme heat in best-of-three-sets singles matches.",
